{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:descent:0347:paragraph/0003", "hash": "sha256:2d18abe21528220d53fcfd6b8cf96427c9ba942a19410e3576f04e180f269731", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 175156, "byte_start": 174776, "file": "descent.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:6cb304635ea274a239d231303eec242d8a4be79a4699f4f2298af5bb2264fe59", "line_end": 4650, "line_start": 4644}, "owner_tag": "0347", "parent_tag": "0347", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0347", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf49cd38737ced1ceba047665de09e9f672cb73fdd7def0d10cc3bcb55ae43ce", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nFinally, we say that a property is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>local for the flat topology<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif it ascends along flat morphisms and descends along flat surjective\nmorphisms. A somewhat silly example is the property of having residue\nfields of a given characteristic. To be more precise, and to tie this in\nwith the various topologies on schemes, we make the following\nformal definition.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d88734d3060d2d300b48cef63d46b8a94c4855855fb351202dad27e011be148a", "unit_id": "inventory:descent:0347:paragraph/0003"}}}, {"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:descent:0347:paragraph/0004", "hash": "sha256:c47f770e9fe7630eef374306653ea0c36fa70920c7bee36ceecf7f5ebfdd973b", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 176246, "b